{"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"=== PR 2 body ===\nAdds `src/adapters/opencode.ts`, wired into `cledger hook`, `cledger capture`, `cledger install`, `renormalize`, and the public library surface.\n\n## Why it looks different from the other two\n\nopencode is the first source with no append-only transcript file — sessions live in a mutable SQLite DB at `~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db`. Rather than read that DB, capture shells out to `opencode export --pure <id>`:\n\n- cledger has zero runtime deps and supports Node >= 20; `node:sqlite` would force both to change.\n- The schema is visibly mid-migration (an empty `session_message` table sits beside the populated `message`/`part` tables it evidently replaces).\n- That same DB holds `credential.value` and `account.access_token`. Reading conversations shouldn't mean opening the file that stores API tokens.\n\n`--sanitize` is deliberately not passed — cledger does its own redaction, and letting opencode rewrite content would make event ids depend on opencode's version.\n\n## Design decisions\n\n**One event per part, not per message.** The store is mutable and a message accumulates parts over time. A part is the finest unit that stops changing, so a message that gains parts after an early `session.idle` appends rather than re-emitting changed content under a new id. Unsettled (`running`) tool calls are skipped *and* hold the cursor back, so they're captured once they finish rather than skipped forever.\n\n**Reasoning is visible, not opaque.** opencode stores reasoning as plain text, unlike Codex's provider-encrypted `encrypted_content`. So it becomes an ordinary `thinking` block in a `conversation_turn` — no opacity marker, nothing withheld.\n\n**Model recorded on user messages too.** opencode states the model on user messages; claude-code doesn't, and there none is invented. Here the source states it, so it's recorded.\n\n**Conservative type classification.** Only `text`/`reasoning`/`tool` are claimed convertible and only `step-start`/`step-finish`/`patch` deliberately skipped. The `file`, `agent`, `snapshot` and `todo` types opencode's binary references are left unclassified on purpose — they route through the drift path (preserved raw-only, warned about, upgradeable by `cledger renormalize`) instead of being discarded on speculation.\n\n**Subagent sessions skipped**, matching claude-code's sidechain handling. Doing it properly is a cross-adapter schema question, now on the roadmap.\n\n## Upstream bug worked around\n\n`opencode export` exits without draining a piped stdout, silently truncating at ~64KB — and the truncated JSON can still parse, so this would have quietly captured partial conversations. The child now writes to a temp file. Verified: 65516 bytes over a pipe vs 446703 to a file descriptor.\n\n## Verification\n\n- 170 tests pass (169 + 1 pre-existing skip), including 5 new adapter tests covering conversion, drift preservation, `occurred_at` fallbacks, idempotent re-capture, unsettled-tool cursor hold, subagent skip, and tool errors.\n- End-to-end against a real 378KB opencode session: 18 events, matching the source part histogram exactly (11 tool, 5 reasoning, 2 text), re-capture appends 0.\n- The generated plugin loads inside real opencode with no errors; install is idempotent.\n\n## Known gaps (on the roadmap)\n\n- `conversation.seq` is positional over a mutable store, so a `session revert` can shift positions and duplicate the parts after the deletion. Per-part capture keeps the blast radius small.\n- The plugin reads `session.idle`'s session id defensively across several key names — opencode's `Event` union isn't in the installed SDK typings and a live event capture couldn't be completed. Falls back to the most recently updated session for the directory.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01YZSeAzTwQ9ikr7D6aiZ8vq\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.cl